namespace UObjectToolTips

DreamShape {
    at    Source/DreamGUIExtensions/Public/Extensions/DreamShape.h#DreamShape
    src   "A filled polygon through any points you give it: triangles, slanted bars, arrows, cursor slashes, star bursts.\n`.dui` tag `Shape`.\n\n    Shape Slash {\n        Points = [(0, 0.2), (1, 1), (0.85, 0.35)]     // normalized, (0,0) bottom left, y up\n        Color = #FF1E3C\n    }\n\nPolygon draws regular N-gons only (each vertex can move along its own ray, never sideways), so a parallelogram or an\narbitrary triangle cannot be made from it. This visual takes the outline directly. The outline is a simple polygon\n-- convex or concave, either winding, no self-intersections -- and is filled by ear clipping. The brush paints it\nthe way it paints an Image: the texture (or material) is laid over the widget's rect and each point samples where it\nsits in that rect, so a shape cut from a picture keeps the picture in place.\n\nPointsTo morphs the outline into another with the same number of points, which is how a cursor stretches from one\nitem to the next. Hit-testing is the rect's, like every other image-derived visual."
}

DreamShape:Points {
    at    Source/DreamGUIExtensions/Public/Extensions/DreamShape.h#DreamShape:Points
    src   "The outline, in order around the shape. Fewer than three points draws nothing."
}

DreamShape:PointsTo {
    at    Source/DreamGUIExtensions/Public/Extensions/DreamShape.h#DreamShape:PointsTo
    src   "Morph from the current outline to InPoints. With a different point count there is nothing to pair the points\nby, so the outline is replaced at once and no tween is returned."
}

EDreamShapePointUnit {
    at    Source/DreamGUIExtensions/Public/Extensions/DreamShape.h#EDreamShapePointUnit
    src   "What a Shape's points are measured in."
}

EDreamShapePointUnit.Normalized {
    at    Source/DreamGUIExtensions/Public/Extensions/DreamShape.h#EDreamShapePointUnit:Normalized
    src   "0..1 across the widget's rect, (0,0) at the bottom left -- the shape stretches with the rect."
}

EDreamShapePointUnit.Pixels {
    at    Source/DreamGUIExtensions/Public/Extensions/DreamShape.h#EDreamShapePointUnit:Pixels
    src   "Pixels from the rect's bottom-left corner -- the shape keeps its size when the rect changes."
}